From 7fc7513ca0b336497006e3693c9941920931d5ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:37:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gresolv: Do not sort an empty result list

A DNS reply without a usable A or AAAA record leaves the lookup with no
results, so rfc3484_sort_results() called qsort() with a NULL array.
That is undefined behaviour even for zero elements, and UBSan reports it.
Found by fuzzing parse_response() with an empty NOERROR reply.

Only sort when there are at least two results.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gweb/gresolv.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gweb/gresolv.c b/gweb/gresolv.c
index b5051ce..f32106d 100644
--- a/gweb/gresolv.c
+++ b/gweb/gresolv.c
@@ -451,8 +451,10 @@ static void rfc3484_sort_results(struct resolv_lookup *lookup)
 		res->src_scope = addr_scope(&res->src.sa);
 	}
 
-	qsort(lookup->results, lookup->nr_results,
-			sizeof(struct sort_result), rfc3484_compare);
+	/* results is NULL when the reply had no usable address */
+	if (lookup->nr_results > 1)
+		qsort(lookup->results, lookup->nr_results,
+				sizeof(struct sort_result), rfc3484_compare);
 }
 
 static void sort_and_return_results(struct resolv_lookup *lookup)
-- 
